⚠️ **IMPORTANT: verdict records are unauthenticated — any PR participant can forge one and steer the machine loop**

`extractVerdictRecord` accepts the marker from ANY comment, regardless of author:

```js
var start = text.indexOf(MARKER_PREFIX);
...
try { parsed = JSON.parse(raw); } catch (e) { return null; }
if (!parsed || !parsed.head || !parsed.verdict) return null;
```

The comment payload carries `author`/`created_at` (the doc even says "accepted but not required"), but the reader never checks it. The marker format is public (this repo), so anyone with comment access to a machine-loop PR can post a newer record than the legs':

- a forged `APPROVE` (newest timestamp) makes `armReworkDecision` withhold rework arms and turns the `latestVerdict: [APPROVE]` reconcile shapes into label strippers — a legitimate red-free `agent:rework` arm placed by the RC verdict comes off on the next tick;
- a forged `APPROVE` defeats the `notLatestVerdict` lanes, un-blocking `pr_approved`-gated validation/merge paths the real review had locked.

The blast radius is bounded — the machine grants no label from records (only `postPRReviewComments` adds `pr_approved`), `merge-validated` still needs machine-owned `ai_validating` + green + CLEAN, and reconciliation only removes labels — so this is automation sabotage / loop stalling, not a merge bypass. But it is a new unauthenticated input channel into state that previously only the machine could write.

Suggested hardening (small): trust only records authored by the machine identity — `parseVerdictRecords`/`extractVerdictRecord` already receives the payload; filter on `item.user.login === machineAuthor` (or the reviewing identity) in `smProvider.verdictRecords`/`readVerdictRecords` before parsing, fail-open to `[]` like the other paths. Add a forge-replay test (non-machine-author record → ignored) alongside the AC4 free-form one.

